---
arrangement: why-improvement-ran-blind
when-used: The IMPROVEMENTS reason line for a command that ran because nothing could check it. Value: the command word.
why: 28G strawman a-fire-morning: the recurring cost is named as a recurring cost (`as on every apply`), which is what makes the improvement worth buying. The strawman says `is undescribed`; this seat cannot yet tell an UNdescribed tool from one whose author deliberately DECLINED this invocation (the anti-nag case, 28G strawman c-declined-unsound), and asserting the wrong one is a mis-attribution (271 rul-sin-ordering), so it states only the engine's own position.
---
-- book.sh --
#!/bin/sh
# Two un-oracled commands and nothing described: the whole run is unprobed, which is exactly the
# world the IMPROVEMENTS panel exists to report. `hork` is the corpus's inert stand-in mutator.
hork tune --profile web
apt-get install -y nginx

